<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) & Gros et al. (2010) vertebrate limb bud oriented cell division & Wnt5a/FGF8 pushing vs proliferation-gradient hypothesis — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module header maps Laws 1-5 to the five Lean theorems and states the two-layer model structure (L29-83); the Section 5 header (L722-743) writes the governing system, BCs and the scope reduction; every FEM function docstring names the paper equation or oracle it implements; panel titles label Panels C-J as the Pass 2 reduced model; `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.yaml` registers Laws 4-5 with lean_locus and code_locus. Not higher because the Pass 2 coefficients in `simulate_limb_bud_regime` are disclosed as fitted but not individually derived or sourced." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py L346–L352: Pass 2 rate coefficients 0.352, 0.560, 0.580, 0.0175, 0.0268 disclosed as calibrated, origin not derived <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L346-L352>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) & Gros et al. (2010) vertebrate limb bud oriented cell division & Wnt5a/FGF8 pushing vs proliferation-gradient hypothesis — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Section 5 now implements the governing equations of Boehm et al. (2010) Eqs. (3)-(5)/(10)-(11) in 3D: P1-P1 stabilised Stokes with distributed source, traceless extensile oriented-division stress integrated by parts, AER-FGF8 body force, traction-free ectoderm and flank Dirichlet/ALE plane (`assemble_stokes_p1p1`/`solve_stokes_growth`, L878-955), verified to round-off against two closed-form oracles (L957-984; Lean Theorem 4) with a Lagrangian RK2 volume budget closed to 0.5 % (L989-1095; Lean Theorem 5); the Model I conclusion of the paper is reproduced parameter-free (+5.21 % PD, band 3.4-11.8 %). Scored down from 94 because (a) the Pass 2 solver that v2 credited as a \"continuum artificial-compressibility Stokes velocity solver\" is a boundary-advection model with Pass-2-fitted coefficients (0.352, 0.560, 0.580, ...) uncoupled from the Poisson field (`simulate_limb_bud_regime`, L336-360 disclosure), and it still produces Panels C-J and 8 of 20 measurements; (b) viscosity/Reynolds dependence exists only as the phenomenological `re_factor` (L270-273), so the \"5-decade Re insensitivity\" is not a property of the solved physics; (c) the active-stress Model II solved faithfully contracts AP/DV against the data, which the file reports rather than hides (L1145-1222)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py L270–L273: Reynolds dependence of the 2D model is a phenomenological re_factor = 0.52 + 0.24 (log Re + 6); the 3D Stokes FEM is Re-independent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L270-L273>",
        "2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py L336–L360: Disclosure that the Pass 2 2D model is a calibrated boundary-advection model, not coupled to the Poisson solver; still drives Panels C-J <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L336-L360>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) & Gros et al. (2010) vertebrate limb bud oriented cell division & Wnt5a/FGF8 pushing vs proliferation-gradient hypothesis — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1788-2016) returns 20 measurements: 12 new FEM metrics (oracle error 8.2e-14, mesh convergence 0.018 pp, Model I PD 5.21 % vs ref 10.1 %, Model I volume ratio 1.123 vs OPT 1.659, WT PD 42.20 % [fitted], WT AP -10.9 % vs +12 %, Wnt5a-/- 11.97 % vs 18.5 % [out-of-sample], FEM 5-regime r 0.9944, v_in* 61.4 um/h, influx PD 42.16 %, and two specimen-derived IoUs 0.770 / 0.847) plus the 8 Pass 2 metrics (2D r 0.9951 after the T_c fix). Both agreement and disagreement with the reference are recorded. Scored down from 95 because 2 of 5 FEM regimes are calibration targets, the 2D r = 0.9951 is a Pass 2 fit, and 4 of 20 measurements are specimen-derived." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py L1853–L1891: WT PD is a calibration target and the 5-regime FEM r counts it; out-of-sample RMSE is 5.3 pp <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L1853-L1891>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-5-regime-6h-pd-elongation-hierarchy-pearson-r-vs-empirical>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-5-regime-e11-5-aspect-ratio-l-pd-w-ap-pearson-r-vs-empirical>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-5-regime-6h-pd-elongation-pearson-r-vs-empirical-2-of-5-regimes-calibrated>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-flank-influx-velocity-v-in-closing-the-opt-6h-volume-gap-model-i-source-only>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-mesh-convergence-of-model-i-pd-elongation-default-466-nodes-fine-1198-nodes>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-model-i-6h-pd-elongation-measured-iddu-brdu-s-x-only-stokes-pinned-flank>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-model-i-6h-volume-ratio-v-st1-v-st0-from-measured-proliferation-alone>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-model-i-flank-influx-v-in-6h-pd-elongation-no-active-stress>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-model-ii-wt-6h-ap-width-change-out-of-sample>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-model-ii-wt-6h-pd-elongation-calibration-target-k-zeta-fitted>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-stokes-manufactured-solution-max-relative-error-uniform-dilation-extensile-stress-oracles>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-fem-wnt5a-zeta-0-12-chi-0-25-6h-pd-elongation-out-of-sample>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-hooke-jeeves-inverse-opt-to-empirical-distal-source-ratio-s-opt-1-s-emp-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-model-i-isotropic-proliferation-6h-pd-elongation-at-re-10-2-negative-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-model-ii-wild-type-6h-pd-elongation-vs-opt-st0-st1-benchmark>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-reynolds-number-5-decade-sensitivity-span-re-in-10-6-10-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-specimen-panel-d-vs-panel-e-3d-opt-iso-surface-aspect-ratio-gain>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-specimen-panel-f-posterior-dv-pd-st1-st0-elongation-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-measurement-specimen-st1-dorsal-silhouette-iou-fem-model-i-flank-influx-v-in-vs-specimen-hull>,
