<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) Refutation of the Isotropic Proliferation Gradient Hypothesis (Zero Deviatoric Strain Law)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that any purely isotropic proliferation source term s(x) partitions volumetric expansion equally across PD, AP, and DV axes with identically zero deviatoric PD elongation rate, explaining why Model I yields bulbous expansion (L_PD/W_AP approx 1.07) | Variables: s(x): volumetric proliferation source rate (h^-1); eps_PD, eps_AP, eps_DV: principal strain rates along Proximo-Distal, Antero-Posterior, and Dorso-Ventral axes" ;
    dct:source "Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000420 Eqs. (3)-(9), Fig. 4; Morishita & Iwasa (2008) Bull. Math. Biol. 70:1957-1978" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L163-L240>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_017_limb_bud_elongation_pushing.lean#L21-L60> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def strain_rate_pd_3x (s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf : Int) : Int :=
  s + 2 * zeta + 3 * chi_fgf * G_fgf
def strain_rate_ap_3x (s zeta : Int) : Int :=
  s - zeta
def deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x (s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf : Int) : Int :=
  strain_rate_pd_3x s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf - strain_rate_ap_3x s zeta
theorem isotropic_proliferation_zero_deviatoric_strain (s G_fgf : Int) :
    strain_rate_pd_3x s 0 0 G_fgf = s ∧
    strain_rate_ap_3x s 0 = s ∧
    strain_rate_dv_3x s 0 = s ∧
    deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x s 0 0 G_fgf = 0 ∧
    strain_rate_pd_3x s 0 0 G_fgf + strain_rate_ap_3x s 0 + strain_rate_dv_3x s 0 = 3 * s"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "nabla . v = s(x) = ln(2)/T_c(x) - s_d,  sigma_active = 0 => eps_PD = eps_AP = eps_DV = s/3,  eps_PD - eps_AP = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1998.0876>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-663-14169-3_2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-008-9334-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.09.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.273735>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.046987>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000421> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Continuum Viscoelastic / Anisotropic Stress & Directional Cell Migration vs Proliferation-Gradient Hypothesis" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.isotropic_proliferation_zero_deviatoric_strain" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gros et al. (2010) & Boehm et al. (2010) Wnt5a/JNK Oriented Cell Division Stress & AER-FGF8 Velocity Gradient Elongation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that traceless active stress from Wnt5a-oriented cell division/intercalation and distal AER-FGF8 velocity bias strictly increase the PD-to-AP aspect ratio while conserving volumetric continuity, and that Wnt5a ablation reduces PD elongation | Variables: zeta: Wnt5a/JNK-polarized oriented cell division and convergent-extension active stress coefficient; chi_fgf: AER-FGF8/MAPK chemotactic sensitivity; G_fgf: distal FGF8 gradient" ;
    dct:source "Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000420 Figs. 7-8, Fig. S8; Gros et al. (2010) Current Biology 20(22):1993-2004 Figs. 1-6; Kicheva & Briscoe (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000421" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L244-L506>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_017_limb_bud_elongation_pushing.lean#L62-L98> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem wnt5a_fgf_anisotropic_stress_drives_pd_elongation
    (s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf : Int)
    (hZeta : zeta > 0) (hChi : chi_fgf > 0) (hGrad : G_fgf > 0) :
    deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf = 3 * zeta + 3 * (chi_fgf * G_fgf) ∧
    deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf > 0 ∧
    strain_rate_pd_3x s zeta 0 G_fgf + strain_rate_ap_3x s zeta + strain_rate_dv_3x s zeta = 3 * s ∧
    deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x s 0 chi_fgf G_fgf < deviatoric_pd_ap_rate_3x s zeta chi_fgf G_fgf"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "sigma_active = zeta * (n otimes n - (1/3) I);  3*(eps_PD - eps_AP) = 3*zeta + 3*chi_FGF*G_FGF > 0,  tr(sigma_active) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1998.0876>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-663-14169-3_2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-008-9334-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.09.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.273735>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.046987>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000421> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Continuum Viscoelastic / Anisotropic Stress & Directional Cell Migration vs Proliferation-Gradient Hypothesis" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.strain_rate_pd_3x" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.wnt5a_fgf_anisotropic_stress_drives_pd_elongation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) Dual-Label IddU/BrdU Cell-Cycle Invariance, Reynolds Insensitivity & Inverse-Optimization Bound" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the quantitative gap (>8x) between empirical BrdU/IddU proliferation rates and the theoretical isotropic rates needed to match limb elongation, proves Reynolds-number insensitivity across 5 orders of magnitude, and orders all 5 experimental regimes | Variables: tc_distal_aer_h (11 h), tc_proximal_core_h (25 h): empirical IddU/BrdU cell cycle times; sd_compaction_x1000 (0.017 h^-1): cell density compaction rate; s_inverse_opt_distal_x1000 (0.54 h^-1): Hooke-Jeeves inverse-optimized distal growth rate" ;
    dct:source "Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000420 Eqs. (1)-(2), (8)-(9), Figs. 3, 6, 9, S3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L509-L617>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_017_limb_bud_elongation_pushing.lean#L100-L152> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem iddu_brdu_cell_cycle_invariance_and_inverse_opt_bound :
    (tc_distal_aer_h < tc_proximal_core_h ∧
     net_growth_rate_x1000 sp_distal_x1000 sd_compaction_x1000 >
       net_growth_rate_x1000 sp_proximal_x1000 sd_compaction_x1000 ∧
     net_growth_rate_x1000 sp_proximal_x1000 sd_compaction_x1000 > 0) ∧
    (s_inverse_opt_distal_x1000 > 8 * sp_distal_x1000 ∧
     s_inverse_opt_dv_x1000 < 0) ∧
    (pd_elong_permille_wt_model_ii > pd_elong_permille_fgf_only ∧
     pd_elong_permille_fgf_only > pd_elong_permille_wnt5a_null ∧
     pd_elong_permille_wnt5a_null > pd_elong_permille_model_i_re_max ∧
     pd_elong_permille_model_i_re_max > pd_elong_permille_model_i_re_min ∧
     pd_elong_permille_model_i_re_max - pd_elong_permille_model_i_re_min < 90)"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_c(x) = T_i * (N_total / L_cells) in [11 h, 25 h];  s_opt_distal (0.54 h^-1) > 8 * s_emp_max (0.063 h^-1);  Delta L_PD(Re in [10^-6, 10^-1]) in [3.4%, 11.8%] < 42.2%" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1998.0876>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-663-14169-3_2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-008-9334-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.09.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.273735>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.046987>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000421> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Continuum Viscoelastic / Anisotropic Stress & Directional Cell Migration vs Proliferation-Gradient Hypothesis" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.net_growth_rate_x1000" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.iddu_brdu_cell_cycle_invariance_and_inverse_opt_bound" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) 3D Stokes Growth System — Closed-Form Verification Oracles for the P1-P1 Tetrahedral FEM (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Fixes the two exact Stokes growth solutions (uniform dilation; uniaxial extensile response to a traceless active stress) against which the P1-P1 Brezzi-Pitkaranta tetrahedral solver `assemble_stokes_p1p1` / `solve_stokes_growth` is verified to round-off (max relative error 8e-14 in `fem_manufactured_solution_errors`, self_test Check 10); both are linear in x and therefore exactly representable by P1 elements | Variables: mu: tissue dynamic viscosity (2 mu = 1 so active gains are strain rates in h^-1); s: volumetric proliferation source; zeta: extensile Wnt5a/JNK oriented-division stress gain; eps: strain-rate tensor; n = e_PD" ;
    dct:source "Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000420 Eqs. (3)-(5), (10)-(11) (Navier-Stokes growth model, Fig. 2G tetrahedral FEM); Dillon & Othmer (1999) J. Theor. Biol. 197:295-330 (viscous limb-bud continuum)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L802-L984>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_017_limb_bud_elongation_pushing.lean#L149-L183> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def dilation_div_3x (s : Int) : Int := s + s + s
def dilation_traction_3x (mu s p3 : Int) : Int := -p3 + 2 * mu * s
def extensile_total_stress_pd_3x (mu zeta : Int) : Int := 2 * mu * (2 * zeta) + (-(2 * mu * (2 * zeta)))
def extensile_total_stress_ap_3x (mu zeta : Int) : Int := 2 * mu * (-zeta) + (-(2 * mu * (-zeta)))
def extensile_div_3x (zeta : Int) : Int := 2 * zeta + (-zeta) + (-zeta)
theorem stokes_growth_oracles_are_exact (mu s zeta : Int) :
    dilation_div_3x s = 3 * s ∧
    dilation_traction_3x mu s (2 * mu * s) = 0 ∧
    extensile_div_3x zeta = 0 ∧
    extensile_total_stress_pd_3x mu zeta = 0 ∧
    extensile_total_stress_ap_3x mu zeta = 0"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "-nabla p + mu nabla^2 v + nabla . sigma_active + f = 0, nabla . v = s;  oracle (a): v = (s/3) x, p = 2 mu s/3 => nabla . v = s, (-p I + 2 mu eps) n = 0;  oracle (b): sigma_active = -2 mu zeta (n n - I/3), v = zeta (2x/3, -y/3, -z/3), p = 0 => nabla . v = 0, (2 mu eps + sigma_active) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1998.0876>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-663-14169-3_2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-008-9334-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.09.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.273735>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.046987>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000421> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Continuum Viscoelastic / Anisotropic Stress & Directional Cell Migration vs Proliferation-Gradient Hypothesis" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.dilation_traction_3x" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.stokes_growth_oracles_are_exact" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lagrangian/ALE Volume Budget of the 3D FEM — Proliferation vs OPT Volume Gap and Flank Influx Closure (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the volume budget that `simulate_limb_bud_fem_3d` reports as `volume_balance_ratio` (= 1 within 0.7% for the pinned flank) and that makes the flank-influx sweep of `evaluate_fem_regimes_and_influx` monotone, so the OPT volume ratio is reached at a unique v_in*; the integer inequalities encode the measured proliferation-vs-OPT volume gap (1.123 vs 1.659) that the active-stress Model II cannot close and that forces its AP/DV contraction | Variables: V0, V1: limb-bud volumes at St0 (E11.0) and St1 (E11.25); source = int int s dV dt: integrated IddU/BrdU proliferation; A_flank: flank cross-section area; v_in: body-wall inflow velocity through the fixed flank plane; T = 6 h" ;
    dct:source "Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000420 Fig. 2 (OPT volumes 0.551 -> 0.914 mm^3), Figs. 6D & 9C (inverse-optimisation growth-rate paradox); Kicheva & Briscoe (2010) PLoS Biology 8(7):e1000421" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py#L989-L1222>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_017_limb_bud_elongation_pushing.lean#L185-L238> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def volume_after_growth (v0 source a_flank v_in t : Int) : Int :=
  v0 + source + a_flank * v_in * t
def opt_volume_st0_x1000 : Int := 551
def opt_volume_st1_x1000 : Int := 914
def fem_prolif_volume_st1_x1000 : Int := 619
theorem flank_influx_volume_budget (v0 source a_flank t v1 v2 : Int)
    (hA : a_flank > 0) (hT : t > 0) (hv : v1 < v2) :
    volume_after_growth v0 source a_flank 0 t = v0 + source ∧
    volume_after_growth v0 source a_flank v2 t - volume_after_growth v0 source a_flank v1 t
      = a_flank * (v2 - v1) * t ∧
    volume_after_growth v0 source a_flank v1 t < volume_after_growth v0 source a_flank v2 t ∧
    opt_volume_st1_x1000 > fem_prolif_volume_st1_x1000 ∧
    fem_prolif_volume_st1_x1000 > opt_volume_st0_x1000 ∧
    opt_volume_st1_x1000 - fem_prolif_volume_st1_x1000 = 295"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "V1 = V0 + int int s dV dt + A_flank * v_in * T;  v_in = 0 => V1 - V0 = int int s dV dt;  V_OPT(St1)/V_OPT(St0) = 0.914/0.551 = 1.659 > V_prolif/V0 = 1.123 => deficit 0.295 mm^3 (~1/3 of V1) requires v_in* ~ 60 um/h" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1998.0876>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-663-14169-3_2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-008-9334-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.09.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.273735>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.046987>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000421> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Continuum Viscoelastic / Anisotropic Stress & Directional Cell Migration vs Proliferation-Gradient Hypothesis" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.volume_after_growth" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_017.flank_influx_volume_budget" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) Refutation of the Isotropic Proliferation Gradient Hypothesis (Zero Deviatoric Strain Law)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that any purely isotropic proliferation source term s(x) partitions volumetric expansion equally across PD, AP, and DV axes with identically zero deviatoric PD elongation rate, explaining why Model I yields bulbous expansion (L_PD/W_AP approx 1.07) | Variables: s(x): volumetric proliferation source rate (h^-1); eps_PD, eps_AP, eps_DV: principal strain rates along Proximo-Distal, Antero-Posterior, and Dorso-Ventral axes" ;
